MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 9becf7d9ed3e4454db5aa56b7345d9f1, type: 3}
  m_Name: AgoraCH2Localization_EN
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  chests:
  - chestID: Arte
    chestImage: {fileID: -566849752, guid: cd191b1f2452b4a49936754476ef1e03, type: 3}
    textChest: "Great! This is a piece of truth from\u2026"
    textClueAgora: "To gain true wisdom, you have to remember that there is always
      more than a point of view about what is the truth\u2026 Some truths of life
      are just customs, emotional or intuition based. Arts talk about these kind
      of truths. For example, when Gata Cattana, a spanish poet and rapper, says
      \u201CThe rich and the poor do not love equally\u201D, she is presenting not
      a simple fact, but a state of mind and a statement of intent"
    altarNumber: 2
  - chestID: Historia
    chestImage: {fileID: 394024147, guid: cd191b1f2452b4a49936754476ef1e03, type: 3}
    textChest: "Great! This is a piece of truth from\u2026"
    textClueAgora: To gain true wisdom, you will need 4 parts of congruence. Congruence
      refers to whether this information corresponds to reality. Always check the
      reality to see if the information is true. For example, if you are health-conscious
      and decide to purchase a new brand of breakfast cereal that claims to be made
      entirely from organic ingredients; you can verify this claim. Research the
      brand, and confirm the authenticity of the organic certification to ensure
      that the information is coherent with the reality. This will help you develop
      your critical thinking and your ability to gather, sort and filter information.
    altarNumber: 4
  - chestID: Mates
    chestImage: {fileID: -950423340, guid: cd191b1f2452b4a49936754476ef1e03, type: 3}
    textChest: "Great! This is a piece of truth from\u2026"
    textClueAgora: To gain true wisdom, you will need 3 parts of consistency. Consistency
      refers to whether that information is coherent with other truths. For example,
      in the process of deciding on a future career path, carefully evaluate your
      personal interests, values, and long-term goals, that you know as truths, to
      decide consistently with them. This actions will lead to developing critical
      thinking in your life choices.
    altarNumber: 3
  - chestID: Ciencia
    chestImage: {fileID: -244741445, guid: cd191b1f2452b4a49936754476ef1e03, type: 3}
    textChest: "Great! This is a piece of truth from\u2026"
    textClueAgora: To gain true wisdom, you will need 5 evidences. Evidences are
      proofs or objective facts, which are not debatable because we can all observe
      them. For example, global warming is a phenomenon supported by multiple evidences,
      and one observable impact is the melting of glaciers showed by satellite imagery
      and photographs taken over time. To understand a situation and know if a phenomenon
      is true, first you have to collect facts and, then, critically think on the
      issue
    altarNumber: 5
  - chestID: Humanidades
    chestImage: {fileID: 1253979381, guid: cd191b1f2452b4a49936754476ef1e03, type: 3}
    textChest: "Great! This is a piece of truth from\u2026"
    textClueAgora: 'To gain true wisdom, you will need 1 part of usefulness & 2 parts
      of original/reliable sources. Usefulness refers to the quality of a piece of
      information in relation to an objective. For example, knowing the potential
      consequences of sharing certain content on social media is useful to protect
      oneself from harmful experiences.  Searching for the original source is the
      way to find the truth of a subjective experience. For example, if you want
      to know how someone feels, it is best to ask them directly rather than guessing
      or asking others. '
    altarNumber: 1
  fusionErrorText: "Warning, something is not working\u2026 Try again..."
  fusionSuccessText: "Everyone is important and can make a difference if they follow
    the path of wisdom... That\u2019s why the puzzle remains incomplete, because
    everyone has to do their part: decide how to live and what to live for.... "
